{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the verdant land of Nippon, thou shalt embark on a journey of great wonder and mirth.\n\n\nIn the grand city of Tokyo, the world's most populous metropolis, thou shalt begin thy adventure.\n\n\nAt break of dawn, thou shalt visit the Meiji Shrine, a sacred shrine dedicated to the deified spirits of Emperor Meiji and his empress. Offer prayers for a safe and memorable journey.\n\n\nThen, to the Tsukiji Fish Market, a haven for seafood lovers, thou shalt repair. Gaze upon the array of marine life and partake of the freshest sushi.\n\n\nIn the afternoon, the bustling streets of Shibuya and Harajuku await. Marvel at the scramble crossing and indulge in the eccentric fashion of Takeshita Street.\n\n\nOn the morrow, journey to the old city of Kyoto, the former imperial capital and a city of timeless beauty.\n\n\nAt Fushimi Inari Shrine, climb the famed Senbon Torii, a pathway of a thousand vermilion gates. The shrine is dedicated to the Shinto god of rice and prosperity.\n\n\nIn the afternoon, visit Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, a Zen temple whose top two floors are completely covered in gold leaf.\n\n\nOn the third day, travel to Nara, the ancient capital and a city of great historical significance.\n\n\nAt Todai-ji Temple, behold the Great Buddha, a colossal bronze statue of the Buddha Vairocana.\n\n\nIn the afternoon, stroll through Nara Park, home to over a thousand wild sika deer. Feed them with deer crackers and frolic with these gentle creatures.\n\n\nOn the final day, visit Hiroshima, a city of resilience and peace.\n\n\nAt the Peace Memorial Park, pay tribute to the victims of the atomic bombing.\n\n\nIn the afternoon, take a ferry to Miyajima Island and visit Itsukushima Shrine, a Shinto shrine dedicated to the goddess of the sea and storms.\n\n\nReturn to Tokyo and prepare for thy journey homeward.\n\n\nThy journey to Japan, a l